{"name":"Astronaut","hex":"#445172","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"astronaut","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of the crew of a spaceship or other spacecraft that travels beyond Earth's atmosphere, or someone trained to serve that purpose.\nAn American space traveler, when contrasted against equivalent terms from other countries such as cosmonaut, taikonaut, spationaut, and vyomanaut.","An American space traveler, when contrasted against equivalent terms from other countries such as cosmonaut, taikonaut, spationaut, and vyomanaut."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/astronaut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Astronaut","blocks":[{"text":"An astronaut is a person trained, equipped, and deployed by a human spaceflight program to serve as a commander or crew member of a spacecraft. Although generally reserved for professional space travelers, the term is sometimes applied to anyone who travels into space, including scientists, politicians, journalists, and space tourists. In the United States, it is a designated term used by three agencies: NASA, the FAA, and the military. The term is also used for people who are trained to fly in a spacecraft after passing certain training courses, regardless of their experience of space travel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Bruce_McCandless_II_during_EVA_in_1984.jpg/330px-Bruce_McCandless_II_during_EVA_in_1984.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astronaut","wikidata":"Q11631"},{"title":"Astronaut (Duran Duran album)","blocks":[{"text":"Astronaut is the eleventh studio album by the English pop rock band Duran Duran, released on 28 September 2004 by Epic Records. It was Duran Duran's first studio album since Pop Trash (2000), and the first full album since Seven and the Ragged Tiger (1983) to be recorded by the most famous five-member lineup of the band."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e4/Duran_Duran_-_Astronaut.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astronaut_(Duran_Duran_album)","wikidata":"Q2453076"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Alan_Shepard_in_capsule_aboard_Freedom_7_before_launch.jpg/500px-Alan_Shepard_in_capsule_aboard_Freedom_7_before_launch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Alan_Shepard_in_capsule_aboard_Freedom_7_before_launch.jpg/1280px-Alan_Shepard_in_capsule_aboard_Freedom_7_before_launch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Alan_Shepard_in_capsule_aboard_Freedom_7_before_launch.jpg/500px-Alan_Shepard_in_capsule_aboard_Freedom_7_before_launch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alan Shepard aboard Freedom 7 (1961)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlan_Shepard_in_capsule_aboard_Freedom_7_before_launch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Astronaut_Groups_1_and_2_-_S63-01419.jpg/500px-Astronaut_Groups_1_and_2_-_S63-01419.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Astronaut_Groups_1_and_2_-_S63-01419.jpg/1280px-Astronaut_Groups_1_and_2_-_S63-01419.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Astronaut_Groups_1_and_2_-_S63-01419.jpg/500px-Astronaut_Groups_1_and_2_-_S63-01419.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The first sixteen NASA astronauts to be selected, February 1963. Back row: White, McDivitt, Young, See, Conrad, Borman, Armstrong, Stafford